# =============================================================================
# File        : .gitignore
# Assignment  : DSO202 Assignment 4 - GitOps delivery with Argo CD
# Descriptor  : 1.5.1, 4.2.2 (Listing 1)
# Purpose     : Keep key material and plaintext Secrets out of the repository.
#               Git history is permanent: a value committed once stays readable
#               in history even after the file is deleted, so these patterns
#               must exist BEFORE any secret file is created (first commit).
#               This file is a safety net only - the real protection is that
#               credentials only ever enter Git as SealedSecrets.
# =============================================================================

# Private keys of any kind
*.key

# Sealed Secrets controller key backups (kept in ~/dso202-keys, never here)
*sealing-key*
*.backup.yaml

# Plaintext credential inputs used once by kubeseal, then deleted
secrets-plain/
*-plain.yaml

# Logs and OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
